From ced645a6a26dffed021e948a8f00dd78cac30e5b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NEMO executor <executor@nemo.local>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 11:15:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] coag: Part C -- NEMO vs DustPy vs exact analytic (0D
 coagulation)

run_dustpy_coag.py: DustPy 0D coag matched to NEMO via DustPy's canonical
'Analytical Coagulation Kernels' recipe (Nr=3, compare cell [1]; gas integration
removed + source zeroed; dust drift off; pure sticking; kernel overridden to the
prescribed constant/additive form; grid + exponential IC matched to NEMO).
Validated DustPy-alone vs the EXACT Golovin/constant analytic (not DustPy's
Bessel-free asymptotic): mass conserved to ~1e-16.

compare_dustpy.py: runs NEMO and DustPy on the identical grid/IC/kernel and
overlays both vs exact analytic; grids match to 8e-15. At evolved times NEMO and
DustPy agree to comparable error and both over-diffuse into the large-mass tail
(k=0 scheme, both codes) -- the honest sec:2c claim (comparable to DustPy, not
competitive with a DG solver). Data dumped to figures/coag_dustpy_data/.

Requires: pip install dustpy (v1.0.9 used).
